1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,060
you

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,060
you

3
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:44,200
Krishnamurti in dialogue with Dr. Alan W. Anderson. J. Krishnamurti was born in

4
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:49,400
South India and educated in England. For the past 40 years he has been speaking

5
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:54,400
in the United States, Europe, India, Australia, and other parts of the world.

6
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:59,680
From the outset of his life's work he repudiated all connections with organized

7
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:04,400
religions and ideologies and said that his only concern was to set men

8
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:10,840
absolutely unconditionally free. He is the author of many books, among them the

9
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:16,920
Awakening of Intelligence, The Urgency of Change, Freedom from the Known, and The

10
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:22,640
Flight of the Eagle. This is one of a series of dialogues between Krishnamurti

11
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:26,880
and Dr. Alan W. Anderson, who is professor of religious studies at San

12
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:31,260
Diego State University where he teaches Indian and Chinese scriptures and the

13
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:37,320
oracular tradition. Dr. Anderson, a published poet, received his degree from

14
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:41,960
Columbia University and the Union Theological Seminary. He has been honored

15
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:49,200
with a Distinguished Teaching Award from the California State Universities. Mr.

16
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:56,240
Krishnamurti, in our last conversation we came almost up to the point where we

17
00:01:56,240 --> 00:02:02,760
were about to begin another on the subject of meditation, and I was hoping

18
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:08,440
that today we could share that together. Right, sir.

19
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:31,320
Sir, I do not know if you are aware of the many schools of meditation in India, in

20
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:44,520
Japan, in China, the Zen, and the various Christian contemplative orders, those who

21
00:02:44,520 --> 00:03:00,840
pray endlessly, keep going day after day, and those who wait to receive the grace

22
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:14,560
of God, or whatever they call it. I think, if I may suggest, we should begin

23
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:24,360
not with what is the right kind of meditation, but what is meditation.

24
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,600
Yes.

25
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:34,520
Then we can proceed and investigate together, and therefore share together,

26
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:51,480
this question of meditation, which is the word meaning ponder, hold together, embrace,

27
00:03:51,560 --> 00:04:00,520
consider very, very deeply. All that word is, the meaning of all that is involved in that one word, meditation.

28
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:10,760
If we could start with saying that we really do not know what meditation is.

29
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,760
A very well.

30
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:21,160
If we accept the orthodox, traditional Christian or Hindu or Buddhist meditation,

31
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:29,160
and there are, of course, the meditation among the Muslims as the Sufis,

32
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:37,160
and if we accept that, then it is all based on tradition.

33
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:43,560
If we accept that, then it is all based on tradition.

34
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,080
A. Yes.

35
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:49,720
K. What some others have experienced, and they lay down the method,

36
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:55,960
or the system to practice what they have achieved,

37
00:04:55,960 --> 00:05:02,520
and so there are probably thousands of schools of meditation,

38
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:07,080
and they are proliferating in this country.

39
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:19,160
So, meditate three times a day, think on a word, a slogan, a mantra,

40
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:22,600
and for that you pay thirty-five dollars or a hundred dollars,

41
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:26,360
and then you get some Sanskrit word or some other Greek word,

42
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,240
and you repeat, repeat, repeat.

43
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:36,680
Then there are all those people who practice various forms of breathing,

44
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:40,680
and the practice of Zen,

45
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:56,200
and all that is a form of establishing a routine,

46
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:06,440
a practice that will essentially make the mind dull.

47
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:11,960
Because if you practice, practice, practice,

48
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:16,840
you become a mechanical mind.

49
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:20,600
So, I have never done any of those things,

50
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:25,160
because I saw, I have personally,

51
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:28,120
if I may talk a little about myself,

52
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:33,720
I have watched, attended,

53
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:38,760
went into certain groups of various types, just look.

54
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:41,800
And I said, this isn't it.

55
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:46,120
I discarded it instantly.

56
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:51,800
So, if we could discard all that,

57
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:58,360
discard the Hindu, the Buddhist, the Christian,

58
00:06:58,360 --> 00:07:04,840
and the various importations of meditation by the gurus from India,

59
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:12,760
and the contemplative, all that as a continuance of a tradition

60
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:19,000
which is the carrying over of what others have said,

61
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:24,360
and others' experiences, other illuminations,

62
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:26,040
others' enlightenment, and so on,

63
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:30,520
if we could totally discard all that,

64
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:35,320
their methods, their systems, their practices, their disciplines,

65
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:39,080
because they are all saying truth, or God,

66
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:43,640
or whatever they like to call it, is something over there,

67
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:48,040
you practice in order to get there.

68
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:52,280
That is a fixed thing according to them.

69
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,880
Of course, it must be fixed.

70
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:57,720
If I keep practice in order to get there,

71
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:00,440
that must be static.

72
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:03,080
A. Yes, of course.

73
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,320
Yes, I quite follow.

74
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:10,200
Truth isn't static, isn't a dead thing.

75
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:15,240
A. No, I quite see that.

76
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:22,920
K. So, if we could honestly put away all that

77
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:28,520
and ask what is meditation, not how to meditate.

78
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:32,120
In asking that question, what is meditation,

79
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:36,040
we will begin to find out,

80
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:39,880
we will begin to meditate ourselves.

81
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:41,320
I don't know if I've... A. Yes, you do.

82
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,520
You make yourself very clear.

83
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:46,520
We are back again to the distinction between an activity,

84
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:49,560
the goal of which lies outside the activity,

85
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:52,040
in contrast to the activity...

86
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:55,000
K. ...the end of which is intrinsic to itself.

87
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,720
Yes.

88
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:02,440
So, could we start with saying,

89
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:07,320
I do not know what meditation is?

90
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,960
A. Yes, I'm willing to start there.

91
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:12,440
K. It's really marvellous if we start from there.

92
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,960
A. It certainly is.

93
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:18,600
K. It brings a great sense of humility.

94
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:25,960
A. Also one intuits even from afar, a freedom.

95
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:29,800
K. Yes, yes, that's right. I don't know.

96
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:34,840
That is a tremendous acknowledgement of a freedom

97
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:39,240
from the established known,

98
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:42,280
the established traditions, the established methods,

99
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:46,280
the established schools and practices.

100
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:47,320
A. Exactly.

101
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:51,880
K. I start with something I don't know.

102
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:57,400
For me, that is a great beauty.

103
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:02,280
Then I am free to move.

104
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,320
A. Exactly.

105
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:11,960
K. I'm free to flow or swim in the enquiry.

106
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:14,600
So I don't know.

107
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:20,600
And then from that we can start.

108
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:24,040
First of all,

109
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:35,240
is meditation divorced from daily living?

110
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:40,840
The daily conduct,

111
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:47,400
the daily desires of fulfilment, ambition, greed, envy,

112
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:52,520
the daily competitive, imitative, conforming spirit,

113
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:58,360
the daily appetites, sensuous, sexual,

114
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:01,640
other forms of intellectual and so on,

115
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:05,640
is meditation divorced from all that?

116
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:09,880
Or is meditation

117
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:16,120
flows through all that?

118
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,720
Covers all that, includes all that?

119
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:26,520
Otherwise meditation has no meaning.

120
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,400
A. Yes, I do.

121
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:32,680
This raises an interesting question I'd like to ask you.

122
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:38,120
Perhaps you'd be good enough to help me clarify this.

123
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:42,280
Now, I've never personally undertaken meditation

124
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:48,280
with respect to its ritual character in some traditions,

125
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:57,320
or its monastic and radically methodical approach.

126
00:11:57,320 --> 00:12:00,920
I've read rather deeply in the literatures

127
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:03,800
that have emanated from those practices,

128
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:06,760
and I'm thinking, for instance,

129
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:12,040
of what I've understood from my study

130
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:18,120
of what is called the Hesychast tradition,

131
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:22,920
where what is called the Jesus Prayer is uttered

132
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:27,880
by the monks, particularly on Mount Athos.

133
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:32,040
Lord Jesus Christ, have mercy upon me, a sinner.

134
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:36,680
This is repeated over and over, with, as I understand it,

135
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:42,920
the hope that some day it will become so automatic

136
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:48,280
that perhaps as a modern-day depth psychologist would put it,

137
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:53,720
the unconscious comes into possession of it,

138
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:58,680
so that what I'm doing, whatever that may be,

139
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:04,680
is itself focused entirely on that prayer.

140
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,720
The claim being that when this is achieved,

141
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,920
when I no longer have to utter the prayer in that sense,

142
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:14,680
the prayer is uttering itself in me.

143
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:18,120
K. The same thing, sir, is expressed in India

144
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:21,160
in a different way, which is mantra, you know that,

145
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:28,120
repetition of a sentence or a word,

146
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:34,920
and the repeating loudly first, then silently,

147
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:39,640
then it has entered into your being,

148
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:46,280
and the very sound of it is going on.

149
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:54,200
And from that sound you act, you live,

150
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:57,720
but it's all self-imposed

151
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:01,240
in order to arrive at a certain point.

152
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:05,880
I say, for instance, when you said the prayer,

153
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:09,080
which we just now repeated, sin.

154
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:14,440
I don't accept sin, I don't know what sin is.

155
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:17,480
A. I can just imagine the horror on the faces

156
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:20,680
of those whose ears catch those words.

157
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:23,800
K. Which means they are conditioned,

158
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:27,080
according to a belief,

159
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:31,400
that there is a Jesus, that there is a sin,

160
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:33,320
that they must be forgiven, all that,

161
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:38,120
is just carrying on a tradition.

162
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:44,040
A. This speaks to me very personally.

163
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:46,360
The basis for the decision that I made years ago

164
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,240
not to do one of these things

165
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:52,200
was embodied in your statement a little earlier,

166
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:56,200
namely that it is expected that out of this word,

167
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,880
or out of these words...

168
00:14:57,880 --> 00:15:00,520
K. Out of breathing, out of all that.

169
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:05,160
A. ...will come somehow this permeation of my total being.

170
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:09,320
And the question that arose for me at the time was,

171
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,160
and I'd like you to clarify this,

172
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:16,040
whether you think this question was correct.

173
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:21,240
What arose in my mind was that statement itself,

174
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:25,880
whether the Mantram or the Jesus Prayer,

175
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:29,960
is itself a finite expression. K. Absolutely.

176
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:34,120
A. Therefore, aren't I doing something strange here?

177
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:37,880
And if I somehow attain to anything that's worth attaining to,

178
00:15:37,880 --> 00:15:42,520
it would probably be in spite of that, rather than because of it.

179
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,360
That perhaps was thinking about thought,

180
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,200
but I didn't feel it at the time.

181
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:50,600
I thought that I was making an intuitive response to it,

182
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,840
and therefore I simply wouldn't go ahead.

183
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,040
Yes, please go on.

184
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,720
K. Quite right, sir.

185
00:15:55,720 --> 00:16:03,880
You see, all that implies that there is a path to truth.

186
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:06,440
The Christian path, the Hindu path, the Zen,

187
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:08,760
the various gurus and systems,

188
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:12,040
there is a path to that enlightenment,

189
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:16,280
or to the truth, or to that immeasurable something or other,

190
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,280
and it is there,

191
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:21,000
all that you have to do is keep on, keep on,

192
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,640
walking, walking, walking towards Satan.

193
00:16:23,640 --> 00:16:30,200
That means that thing is established, fixed, static,

194
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:35,800
is not moving, is not living.

195
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:40,040
A. Flashed into my mind the biblical text

196
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:43,640
in which God is described as,

197
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:47,400
the lamp unto my feet and the light unto my path.

198
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:49,640
It doesn't say he is the path,

199
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:52,840
but rather he is the lamp to the path.

200
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:57,560
Right. As a lamp to the feet and a light to the path.

201
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:00,200
But it doesn't say that God is the path.

202
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,360
That's very interesting.

203
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:06,440
But maybe nobody really looks at those words closely.

204
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:11,000
K. You see, sir, how you are looking at it already.

205
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:16,000
You are... that statement...

206
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:22,280
you see the truth of that statement, the feeling of it.

207
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:23,960
A. Yes.

208
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:27,880
K. So, that's one thing.

209
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:36,280
Does meditation cover the whole field of existence?

210
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:41,480
Or is it something totally apart from life?

211
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:46,200
Like being business, politics, sex, pleasure,

212
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:50,240
ambition, greed, envy, anxiety, death, fear,

213
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,280
all that is my life.

214
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:54,520
Life, living.

215
00:17:54,520 --> 00:18:02,200
Is meditation apart from that, or does it embrace all that?

216
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:07,400
If it doesn't embrace all that, meditation has no meaning.

217
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:13,040
A. Something just came to me

218
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:19,560
that I'm sure would be regarded as incredibly heretical.

219
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:24,920
But you know, the words of Jesus himself,

220
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:30,080
I am the way, the truth and the life,

221
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:35,160
when understood in the context of what has been revealed

222
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:37,840
through these discussions we've had,

223
00:18:37,840 --> 00:18:43,080
takes on, in relation to something else he said,

224
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:46,400
an incredibly different meaning from what we've been taught.

225
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:50,240
For instance, when he asks Peter who he is,

226
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:52,880
that is, who am I, Jesus,

227
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,920
and Peter says,

228
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:57,280
Thou art the Christ, the Son of the Living God,

229
00:18:57,280 --> 00:18:59,360
he immediately turns to him and says,

230
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,280
flesh and blood has not revealed this to you.

231
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,000
Nothing to do with flesh and blood,

232
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,800
but my Father which is in heaven,

233
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:09,480
which he says elsewhere, is one with him,

234
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,040
and he's one with the Father.

235
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,800
And then he prays in his prayer

236
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:15,760
that the disciples be one with him,

237
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:18,040
as he and his Father are one,

238
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:21,120
that they all may be one.

239
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:23,800
So if you look at that,

240
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:25,480
I'm almost stuttering over myself,

241
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:27,520
because what I'm about to say,

242
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:30,160
I'm aware of, theologically speaking,

243
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:33,760
would be looked on as fantastical,

244
00:19:33,760 --> 00:19:36,840
when he says, I am the way, the truth and the life,

245
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:43,880
if it's seen in the context of that one as act,

246
00:19:43,880 --> 00:19:51,800
then the whole business utterly is transformed, isn't it?

247
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:54,680
I'm going to be swallowing hard about that for a long time.

248
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,840
Please go on.

249
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,760
So if it is divorced from life,

250
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:01,600
then meditation has no meaning,

251
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:04,920
it's just an escape from life,

252
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:11,000
escape from all our travails and miseries, sorrows, confusion,

253
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:15,200
and therefore it's not worth even touching.

254
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:20,040
A. Yes. Right.

255
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:24,680
K. If it is not, and it is not for me,

256
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:30,680
then what is meditation?

257
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:32,520
You follow?

258
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:39,160
Is it an achievement,

259
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:44,520
an attainment of a goal,

260
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:49,240
or is it a perfume,

261
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:56,240
a beauty that pervades all my activities?

262
00:20:56,240 --> 00:21:01,240
Therefore it has tremendous significance.

263
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:06,120
Meditation has tremendous significance.

264
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:11,120
Then the next question is,

265
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:18,680
is it the result of a search,

266
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:23,880
joining Zen group, then another group,

267
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:26,480
you follow? One after the other,

268
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:29,520
practice this and practice that,

269
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:31,880
take a vow of celibacy, poverty,

270
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:37,480
or don't speak at all, fast,

271
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:42,360
in order to get there?

272
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:48,800
For me, all those are totally unnecessary.

273
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:57,720
Because what is important is,

274
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:03,800
the seeing, as we said yesterday, the false.

275
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:08,680
Not I judge the false as true or false,

276
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:14,840
but the very perception reveals the truth and the falseness of it.

277
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:19,280
I must look at it, my eyes must look at it

278
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:23,960
without any prejudices, without any reactions.

279
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:29,520
Then I can say, this is false, I won't touch it.

280
00:22:29,520 --> 00:22:32,040
That's what I have to...

281
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:34,080
People have come to me and said,

282
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:37,520
you have no idea of all the things.

283
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:41,000
They have said, I said, nothing doing.

284
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:43,760
To me this is false,

285
00:22:43,760 --> 00:22:49,080
because it doesn't include your life.

286
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:53,200
You haven't changed.

287
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:56,480
You may say, I'm full of love, I'm full of truth,

288
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,600
I'm full of knowledge, I'm full of wisdom.

289
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:00,440
That's all nonsense.

290
00:23:00,440 --> 00:23:04,520
Do you behave?

291
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:07,400
Are you free of fear?

292
00:23:07,400 --> 00:23:13,760
Are you free of the ambition, greed, envy, and the desire

293
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:17,080
to achieve success in every field?

294
00:23:17,080 --> 00:23:21,600
If not, you are just playing a game.

295
00:23:21,600 --> 00:23:24,000
You are not serious.

296
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:29,920
So, from that we can proceed.

297
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:37,880
That meditation includes the whole field of existence,

298
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:43,120
whether in the artistic field,

299
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:45,960
or in the business field,

300
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:49,960
because to me the division as the artist,

301
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:53,640
business, the politician, the priest,

302
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,680
the scholar, and the scientist,

303
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:58,920
you know how we have fragmented all this,

304
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:04,000
as careers, to me,

305
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:06,800
as human beings are fragmented,

306
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:13,160
the expression of this fragmentation is this,

307
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:20,240
business, scientist, the scholar, the artist.

308
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:21,640
You? A.S. – Yes, yes, yes.

309
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:24,200
I'm thinking of what goes on in the academy

310
00:24:24,200 --> 00:24:25,360
with respect to this.

311
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:28,440
We are always saying to each other as academicians,

312
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:31,560
for heaven's sake, let's find an ordering principle

313
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:35,920
by which to bring all this into some kind of integration,

314
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:40,840
so the student really can feel

315
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:43,200
that he is doing something meaningful,

316
00:24:43,200 --> 00:24:45,400
and not just adding another freight car

317
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,880
to the long train of what he doesn't even see.

318
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:51,000
K. K. Yes.

319
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:59,400
And meditation must be, or is,

320
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:02,000
when you deny all this

321
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:07,000
– systems, methods, gurus, authorities –

322
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:11,000
becomes a religious question.

323
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:13,000
A.S. – Yes.

324
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:15,000
Profoundly religious question.

325
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:17,000
K. Profoundly religious.

326
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:20,000
Now, what place does meditation have

327
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:25,000
– now, what place has an artist?

328
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:35,000
In the not only social structure,

329
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:41,000
in his expression of the religious.

330
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:44,000
You understand?

331
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:49,000
What is an artist, sir?

332
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:58,000
Is he something apart from our daily living,

333
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:00,000
the beauty of living,

334
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:04,000
the quality of a mind that is really religious?

335
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:05,000
You follow?

336
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Is he part of that, or is he a freak outside that?

337
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:16,000
Because he has certain talents.

338
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,800
And the expression of that talent,

339
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:26,800
becomes extraordinarily important to him and to the people.

340
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:30,800
A. In our culture it often seems

341
00:26:30,800 --> 00:26:32,800
that the expression of that talent

342
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:35,800
brings him into conflict with certain conventions.

343
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:39,800
K. And also expression of that conflict in himself.

344
00:26:39,800 --> 00:26:42,800
A. Of course.

345
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:44,800
Yes, we have a long tradition

346
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:47,800
in Western civilisation of the artist

347
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:49,800
as an outsider, don't we?

348
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:52,800
K. Yes, something outsider.

349
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:56,800
But he is much more sensitive,

350
00:26:56,800 --> 00:27:04,800
much more alert to beauty, to nature.

351
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:09,800
But apart from that, he is just an ordinary man.

352
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:12,800
A. Yes, of course.

353
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:17,800
To me, that is a contradiction.

354
00:27:18,800 --> 00:27:22,800
First be a total human being,

355
00:27:22,800 --> 00:27:24,800
and then whatever you create,

356
00:27:24,800 --> 00:27:27,800
whatever you do will be beautiful.

357
00:27:27,800 --> 00:27:28,800
A. Of course.

358
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:34,800
Whether you paint, whatever you do.

359
00:27:35,800 --> 00:27:40,800
Let's divide the artist into something extraordinary,

360
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:44,800
or the businessman something ugly.

361
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:48,800
The scholar just living in a world of the intellect,

362
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:51,800
or the scientist in the world of physics,

363
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,800
and so on, so on, so on.

364
00:27:53,800 --> 00:27:57,800
But first there must be a human being.

365
00:27:57,800 --> 00:27:58,800
You follow, sir?

366
00:27:58,800 --> 00:28:05,800
Human being in the sense the total understanding of life

367
00:28:05,800 --> 00:28:11,800
– death, love, beauty, relationship, responsibility,

368
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:15,800
not to kill – all that is implied in living.

369
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:22,800
Therefore he establishes a relationship with nature.

370
00:28:22,800 --> 00:28:25,800
And the expression of that relationship,

371
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:30,800
if it is whole, healthy, is creative.

372
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:32,800
A. This is very, very different

373
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:36,800
from what many artists conceive of as their task,

374
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:38,800
especially in modern times.

375
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:42,800
Artists have this notion that they are in some sense

376
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:46,800
reflectors of the fragmentation of their times.

377
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:48,800
And so they make a statement

378
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:53,800
which holds up the fragmentation as a mirror to us.

379
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:55,800
And what has this got to do with anything else

380
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:57,800
but reinforcing the fragmentation?

381
00:28:57,800 --> 00:28:58,800
K. Absolutely.

382
00:28:58,800 --> 00:29:02,800
A. Yes, of course. Yes, I quite understand what you are saying.

383
00:29:02,800 --> 00:29:11,800
K. You see, meditation covers the whole field of existence.

384
00:29:12,800 --> 00:29:19,800
Meditation implies freedom from the method, the system,

385
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:22,800
because I don't know what meditation is.

386
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:24,800
I start from there.

387
00:29:24,800 --> 00:29:29,800
Therefore I start with freedom, not with their burden.

388
00:29:29,800 --> 00:29:30,800
A. That's marvellous.

389
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:33,800
Start with freedom and not with their burden.

390
00:29:33,800 --> 00:29:36,800
This business of holding up fragmentation to us

391
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:37,800
from that perspective

392
00:29:37,800 --> 00:29:40,800
is really nothing more than a species of journalism.

393
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:42,800
K. Absolutely. A. Isn't it? Yes, of course.

394
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:44,800
K. Propaganda. A. Of course.

395
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:49,800
K. Therefore, life.

396
00:29:49,800 --> 00:29:54,800
So I discard all that, so I have no burden.

397
00:29:54,800 --> 00:29:59,800
Therefore the mind is free to enquire what is meditation.

398
00:29:59,800 --> 00:30:01,800
A. Marvellous.

399
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,800
K. To me, I have done this.

400
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:04,800
You follow, sir?

401
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:07,800
This is not verbal expressions.

402
00:30:07,800 --> 00:30:11,800
I don't say anything which I haven't lived.

403
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:13,800
A. Oh, that's very, very obvious to me.

404
00:30:13,800 --> 00:30:16,800
There is one sitting here conversing with you. Yes.

405
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:19,800
That is hypocrisy. I am not interested in all that.

406
00:30:19,800 --> 00:30:24,800
I am really interested in seeing what is meditation.

407
00:30:24,800 --> 00:30:30,800
So one starts with this freedom,

408
00:30:30,800 --> 00:30:35,800
and freedom means the mind emptying itself

409
00:30:35,800 --> 00:30:39,800
of the burdens of others,

410
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:41,800
their methods, their systems,

411
00:30:41,800 --> 00:30:45,800
their acceptance of authority, their beliefs, their hope,

412
00:30:45,800 --> 00:30:48,800
because it is part of me, all that.

413
00:30:48,800 --> 00:30:50,800
Therefore I discard all that.

414
00:30:50,800 --> 00:30:53,800
And now I start by saying,

415
00:30:53,800 --> 00:30:59,800
I don't know what meditation is.

416
00:30:59,800 --> 00:31:08,800
I start, that means the mind has this sense of great humility.

417
00:31:08,800 --> 00:31:12,800
Not knowing, I am not asking.

418
00:31:12,800 --> 00:31:16,800
Then somebody will feel it.

419
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:17,800
A. Exactly.

420
00:31:17,800 --> 00:31:20,800
K. Some book, some scholar, some professor,

421
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:22,800
some psychologist comes along and says,

422
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:24,800
you don't know, I know, I will give it to you.

423
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:28,800
I say, please don't.

424
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:33,800
I know nothing. You know nothing either.

425
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:38,800
Because you are repeating what others have said.

426
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:43,800
So I discard all that.

427
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:45,800
Now I begin to enquire.

428
00:31:45,800 --> 00:31:50,800
I am in a position to enquire.

429
00:31:50,800 --> 00:31:55,800
Not to achieve a result,

430
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:58,800
not to arrive at what they call enlightenment.

431
00:31:58,800 --> 00:32:03,800
Nothing. I don't know if there is enlightenment or not.

432
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:08,800
I start with this feeling of great humility,

433
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:17,800
not knowing, therefore the mind is capable of real enquiry.

434
00:32:18,800 --> 00:32:20,800
So enquire.

435
00:32:20,800 --> 00:32:23,800
First of all, I look at my life,

436
00:32:23,800 --> 00:32:25,800
because I said at the beginning,

437
00:32:26,800 --> 00:32:33,800
meditation implies covering the whole feel of life.

438
00:32:33,800 --> 00:32:36,800
My life, our life,

439
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:41,800
is first I take the daily conscious living.

440
00:32:41,800 --> 00:32:44,800
I have examined, I have looked at it,

441
00:32:44,800 --> 00:32:46,800
there is contradiction and so on,

442
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:48,800
we have been talking about that.

443
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:52,800
And also there is the question of sleep.

444
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:56,800
I go to sleep.

445
00:32:56,800 --> 00:32:59,800
Eight, nine, ten hours.

446
00:32:59,800 --> 00:33:01,800
What is sleep?

447
00:33:01,800 --> 00:33:07,800
I start not knowing, not what others have said.

448
00:33:08,800 --> 00:33:09,800
You follow, sir?

449
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:10,800
A. Yes, I do.

450
00:33:10,800 --> 00:33:14,800
K. I am enquiring in relation to meditation,

451
00:33:14,800 --> 00:33:21,800
which is the real spirit of religion.

452
00:33:21,800 --> 00:33:25,800
That is, gathering all the energy

453
00:33:25,800 --> 00:33:33,800
to move from one dimension to a totally different dimension,

454
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:37,800
which doesn't mean divorce from this dimension.

455
00:33:37,800 --> 00:33:41,800
A. No, it's not like those monks going up the hill.

456
00:33:41,800 --> 00:33:45,800
K. No, I have been up those hills.

457
00:33:45,800 --> 00:33:47,800
A. Yes.

458
00:33:48,800 --> 00:33:54,800
So, what is sleep? And what is waking?

459
00:33:54,800 --> 00:33:58,800
Am I awake?

460
00:33:59,800 --> 00:34:03,800
Or I am only awake when there is a crisis,

461
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:06,800
when there is a shock, when there is a challenge,

462
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:10,800
when there is an incident,

463
00:34:11,800 --> 00:34:16,800
death, discard, failure, you follow?

464
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:19,800
Or am I awake all the time?

465
00:34:19,800 --> 00:34:22,800
In waking, during the daytime.

466
00:34:22,800 --> 00:34:26,800
So, what is to be awake?

467
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:28,800
You are following, sir?

468
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:29,800
A. Yes, I am.

469
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:32,800
Since you are saying meditation must permeate,

470
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:36,800
obviously to be awake cannot be episodic.

471
00:34:36,800 --> 00:34:38,800
K. That's it.

472
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:43,800
Cannot be episodic, cannot be something stimulated.

473
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:46,800
A. Cannot be described as peak experiences.

474
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:52,800
K. Any form of stimulation, external or internal,

475
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:58,800
only implies that you are asleep and you need a stimulant,

476
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:02,800
whether it is coffee, sex, or a tranquiliser,

477
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:04,800
or keep you awake.

478
00:35:04,800 --> 00:35:08,800
A. Have a shock to go to sleep and have a shock to wake up.

479
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:13,800
In my enquiry I am asking, am I awake?

480
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:18,800
What does it mean to be awake?

481
00:35:19,800 --> 00:35:23,800
Not awake to what is happening,

482
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:27,800
politically, economically, socially,

483
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:33,800
that's obvious, but awake, what does it mean?

484
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:37,800
I am not awake if I have any burden.

485
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:40,800
Right, sir?

486
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:43,800
There is no sense of being awake

487
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:47,800
where there is any kind of fear.

488
00:35:47,800 --> 00:35:51,800
If I live in an illusion,

489
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:53,800
if my actions are neurotic,

490
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:58,800
there is no state of being awake.

491
00:35:58,800 --> 00:36:02,800
So, I am enquiring.

492
00:36:02,800 --> 00:36:06,800
And I can only enquire by becoming very sensitive

493
00:36:06,800 --> 00:36:10,800
to what is happening in me outside of me.

494
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:16,800
So, is the mind aware during the day,

495
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:21,800
completely to what is happening inside, outside of me?

496
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:24,800
A. Upon every instant.

497
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:28,800
K. That's it. Otherwise I am not awake.

498
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:30,800
A. I was just thinking about something

499
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:33,800
that has always given me a great sense of wonder.

500
00:36:33,800 --> 00:36:37,800
At home we have some birds, and of all things a cat too.

501
00:36:37,800 --> 00:36:39,800
But they love one another.

502
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:44,800
That is to say, the birds don't run around in the room with the cat,

503
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:47,800
but the cat supervises the birds.

504
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:49,800
When the birds are put to bed in the evening,

505
00:36:49,800 --> 00:36:51,800
the cat goes into that room

506
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:54,800
and stays with them maybe an hour or two, watches,

507
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:56,800
just seems to have the feeling

508
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:59,800
that it must look after the birds.

509
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:02,800
And in the daytime I have often watched the cat sit

510
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:08,800
and look at the birds with an immense intensity.

511
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:10,800
And the ordinary reaction is,

512
00:37:10,800 --> 00:37:14,800
well, for heaven's sake, haven't you seen them before?

513
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:17,800
What is this everlasting intensity?

514
00:37:17,800 --> 00:37:19,800
But she is looking.

515
00:37:19,800 --> 00:37:20,800
K. That's right, sir.

516
00:37:20,800 --> 00:37:29,800
A. And her eyes are always with that jewel-like intensity and clarity,

517
00:37:29,800 --> 00:37:31,800
cleaner than flame.

518
00:37:31,800 --> 00:37:33,800
And it never stops.

519
00:37:33,800 --> 00:37:37,800
And when she sleeps, she really sleeps.

520
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:41,800
Yes. When you ask me, what is sleep,

521
00:37:41,800 --> 00:37:45,800
there must be a relation between the wonder that we feel

522
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:48,800
for the cat's ability completely to sleep,

523
00:37:48,800 --> 00:37:53,800
and when she awakes, she is completely awake.

524
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:54,800
Am I...

525
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:55,800
K. That's right, sir.

526
00:37:55,800 --> 00:37:59,800
So, in asking and inquiring what is sleep,

527
00:37:59,800 --> 00:38:05,800
I must also ask what is to be awake.

528
00:38:05,800 --> 00:38:06,800
A. Of course.

529
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:07,800
K. Of course.

530
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:16,800
Am I awake, or is the past so alive

531
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:20,800
that it is dictating my life in the present?

532
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:24,800
Therefore I must sleep.

533
00:38:24,800 --> 00:38:28,800
A. Would you say that again? That's very important.

534
00:38:29,800 --> 00:38:32,800
I don't know how I... I'll put it differently.

535
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:34,800
Am I awake?

536
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:41,800
Is my mind burdened with the past,

537
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:45,800
and therefore bearing a burden, I am not awake in the present?

538
00:38:45,800 --> 00:38:48,800
A. Not awake in the present. Exactly.

539
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,800
K. Not awake as I am talking.

540
00:38:50,800 --> 00:38:57,800
Because I am talking from the background of my past,

541
00:38:57,800 --> 00:39:03,800
of my experience, of my failures, my hurts, my depressions.

542
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:08,800
Therefore the past is dominating

543
00:39:08,800 --> 00:39:14,800
and putting me to sleep now.

544
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:16,800
A. It's a narcotic. K. Narcotic.

545
00:39:16,800 --> 00:39:18,800
Therefore, what am I to do with the past?

546
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:19,800
You follow, sir?

547
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:21,800
A. Yes, I do. Yes, yes, yes.

548
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:23,800
K. Past is necessary.

549
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:25,800
A. Of course. Yes, the whole field of knowledge.

550
00:39:25,800 --> 00:39:27,800
K. Knowledge. Past is necessary.

551
00:39:27,800 --> 00:39:33,800
But when the past covers the present,

552
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:38,800
then I am asleep.

553
00:39:40,800 --> 00:39:44,800
So, is it possible to keep,

554
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:49,800
to know what the past is

555
00:39:49,800 --> 00:39:54,800
and not let it overflow into the present?

556
00:39:55,800 --> 00:40:00,800
That question and the reality of it

557
00:40:00,800 --> 00:40:04,800
brings its own discipline.

558
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:06,800
Therefore I say, yes, I know what it means.

559
00:40:06,800 --> 00:40:10,800
I can live, I can keep awake totally,

560
00:40:10,800 --> 00:40:16,800
and widely, and yet operate in the field of knowledge.

561
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,800
So there is no contradiction.

562
00:40:18,800 --> 00:40:20,800
I don't know if I am conveying it.

563
00:40:20,800 --> 00:40:22,800
A. Oh, you are. You are.

564
00:40:22,800 --> 00:40:25,800
K. They both are moving in harmony.

565
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:28,800
One doesn't lag behind the other.

566
00:40:28,800 --> 00:40:31,800
One doesn't contradict the other.

567
00:40:31,800 --> 00:40:33,800
That's balance.

568
00:40:33,800 --> 00:40:37,800
A. What I am seeing here, if I am following correctly,

569
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:42,800
is on the one hand we have knowledge

570
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:44,800
and the grasp of its necessity

571
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:47,800
with respect to know-how in practical affairs.

572
00:40:47,800 --> 00:40:51,800
On the other hand we have seeing, understanding,

573
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:58,800
and the act of meditation is the nexus between them,

574
00:40:58,800 --> 00:41:02,800
so that there is no interruption of flow

575
00:41:02,800 --> 00:41:05,800
in the activity of understanding and knowing.

576
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:08,800
K. That is part of meditation. A. Of course.

577
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:12,800
K. You follow? Now see what is taking place.

578
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:13,800
Then what is sleep?

579
00:41:13,800 --> 00:41:17,800
I have understood now what it means to be awake.

580
00:41:17,800 --> 00:41:20,800
That means I am watching.

581
00:41:21,800 --> 00:41:23,800
I am aware.

582
00:41:23,800 --> 00:41:26,800
I am aware without any choice, choiceless awareness,

583
00:41:26,800 --> 00:41:30,800
watching, looking, observing, hearing

584
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:32,800
what is going on, what is going on outside,

585
00:41:32,800 --> 00:41:34,800
what people tell me, whether they flatter me,

586
00:41:34,800 --> 00:41:37,800
whether they insult me, I am watching.

587
00:41:37,800 --> 00:41:41,800
So I am very aware.

588
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:44,800
Now, what is sleep?

589
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:46,800
I know what is sleep.

590
00:41:46,800 --> 00:41:49,800
Resting, shutting your eyes, going to bed,

591
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:54,800
at nine or ten or later.

592
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:56,800
What is sleep?

593
00:41:56,800 --> 00:42:01,800
And in sleep, dreams. What are dreams?

594
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:04,800
I don't know what the others say.

595
00:42:04,800 --> 00:42:08,800
I am not interested in what the others say.

596
00:42:08,800 --> 00:42:09,800
You follow, sir?

597
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:13,800
Because my enquiry is to find out

598
00:42:13,800 --> 00:42:16,800
whether meditation covers the whole field of life,

599
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:18,800
not just one segment.

600
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:21,800
A. My enquiry is from the point where I say,

601
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:22,800
I don't know.

602
00:42:22,800 --> 00:42:25,800
K. I don't know. That's right. So I proceed.

603
00:42:25,800 --> 00:42:30,800
I dream. There are dreams. What are dreams?

604
00:42:31,800 --> 00:42:34,800
Why should I dream?

605
00:42:34,800 --> 00:42:37,800
So I have to find out why I dream. What are dreams?

606
00:42:37,800 --> 00:42:45,800
Dreams are the continuation of my daily sleep.

607
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:51,800
Which is, I haven't understood

608
00:42:51,800 --> 00:42:52,800
– see what is taking place, sir –

609
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:54,800
I haven't understood my daily life,

610
00:42:54,800 --> 00:42:58,800
I haven't watched my daily life.

611
00:42:58,800 --> 00:43:03,800
My daily life is in disorder.

612
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:09,800
So I go to sleep and the disorder continues.

613
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:15,800
And the brain says, I must have order,

614
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:19,800
otherwise I can't function.

615
00:43:19,800 --> 00:43:25,800
So if the mind doesn't put order during the day,

616
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:30,800
the brain tries to bring order during the night.

617
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:31,800
I don't know if you understand.

618
00:43:31,800 --> 00:43:32,800
A. Through the dream.

619
00:43:32,800 --> 00:43:37,800
K. Through dreams, through intimations.

620
00:43:37,800 --> 00:43:38,800
When I wake up I say,

621
00:43:38,800 --> 00:43:43,800
yes, I have a certain feeling this must be done.

622
00:43:43,800 --> 00:43:47,800
So, see what takes place.

623
00:43:47,800 --> 00:43:53,800
When the mind is awake during the day, it has order.

624
00:43:53,800 --> 00:43:55,800
It has established order,

625
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:58,800
in the order in the sense we have discussed previously.

626
00:43:58,800 --> 00:43:59,800
A. Yes, in that sense of order.

627
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:05,800
Order which comes out of the understanding of disorder.

628
00:44:05,800 --> 00:44:09,800
The negation of disorder is order,

629
00:44:09,800 --> 00:44:12,800
not the following of a blueprint,

630
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:16,800
or a pattern, or all that, is disorder.

631
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:22,800
So during the day the mind, the brain has established order.

632
00:44:22,800 --> 00:44:28,800
So when I sleep the brain isn't working out

633
00:44:28,800 --> 00:44:34,800
how to establish order in itself in order to be secure.

634
00:44:34,800 --> 00:44:39,800
Therefore the brain becomes rested.

635
00:44:39,800 --> 00:44:45,800
Therefore the brain becomes quiet, sleeps without dreams.

636
00:44:45,800 --> 00:44:47,800
It may have superficial dreams,

637
00:44:47,800 --> 00:44:50,800
when you eat wrongly, you know, all that kind of thing,

638
00:44:50,800 --> 00:44:53,800
but I am not talking about that.

639
00:44:53,800 --> 00:44:59,800
Sleep means regeneration of the brain.

640
00:44:59,800 --> 00:45:00,800
A. Yes, I do.

641
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:04,800
I wonder if I could ask you a question about dreams here,

642
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:10,800
that might introduce a distinction between dreams

643
00:45:10,800 --> 00:45:14,800
in terms of their nature.

644
00:45:14,800 --> 00:45:19,800
Sometimes we report that we have had a dream

645
00:45:19,800 --> 00:45:22,800
which points to a future event.

646
00:45:22,800 --> 00:45:25,800
That's entirely different from what you are talking about.

647
00:45:25,800 --> 00:45:27,800
So we could say that...

648
00:45:27,800 --> 00:45:31,800
K. Sir, I think that we can understand that fairly simply.

649
00:45:31,800 --> 00:45:39,800
You know, the other day we were walking high up in the hills in India,

650
00:45:39,800 --> 00:45:42,800
and there was a river flowing down below,

651
00:45:42,800 --> 00:45:46,800
and two boats were coming in the opposite direction,

652
00:45:46,800 --> 00:45:48,800
and you knew where they were going to meet.

653
00:45:48,800 --> 00:45:52,800
A. Of course.

654
00:45:54,800 --> 00:45:56,800
K. When you go high enough,

655
00:45:56,800 --> 00:46:01,800
you see the boats coming together at a precise point.

656
00:46:01,800 --> 00:46:03,800
A. But that's very objective.

657
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:07,800
That has nothing to do with my subjective unfinished business,

658
00:46:07,800 --> 00:46:09,800
which is the other thing you were talking about.

659
00:46:09,800 --> 00:46:12,800
Yes, I quite say.

660
00:46:12,800 --> 00:46:15,800
A. What an amazing thing it would be

661
00:46:15,800 --> 00:46:18,800
to have all your business done and go to sleep,

662
00:46:18,800 --> 00:46:26,800
and if order should present you with an understanding,

663
00:46:26,800 --> 00:46:29,800
then the understanding never stops from waking through sleep.

664
00:46:29,800 --> 00:46:32,800
K. That's right. A. Yes, of course.

665
00:46:32,800 --> 00:46:33,800
Marvellous.

666
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:40,800
K. So you see, that way the brain is regenerated,

667
00:46:40,800 --> 00:46:44,800
keeps young, no conflict.

668
00:46:44,800 --> 00:46:47,800
Conflict wears out the brain.

669
00:46:47,800 --> 00:46:50,800
A. Yes.

670
00:46:50,800 --> 00:47:01,800
K. So, sleep means not only order, rejuvenation, innocence,

671
00:47:01,800 --> 00:47:06,800
but also there are, in sleep,

672
00:47:06,800 --> 00:47:13,800
there are states in which there is absolutely freedom to enquire,

673
00:47:13,800 --> 00:47:19,800
to see into something that you have never seen with your physical eyes.

674
00:47:19,800 --> 00:47:20,800
A. Yes.

675
00:47:20,800 --> 00:47:22,800
K. Of course.

676
00:47:22,800 --> 00:47:27,800
So, we have described sufficiently into that. I see that.

677
00:47:27,800 --> 00:47:35,800
So does the mind live that kind of life during the day?

678
00:47:35,800 --> 00:47:38,800
A. That would be rare. K. Otherwise it's not meditation.

679
00:47:38,800 --> 00:47:41,800
A. Otherwise it's not meditation. Of course.

680
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:43,800
K. And I don't want to play a hypocritical game,

681
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:46,800
because I am deceiving nobody, I am deceiving myself,

682
00:47:46,800 --> 00:47:48,800
and I don't want to deceive myself.

683
00:47:48,800 --> 00:47:52,800
I don't see the point of deceiving oneself.

684
00:47:52,800 --> 00:47:55,800
Because I don't want to be a great man, little man, big man,

685
00:47:55,800 --> 00:47:59,800
success and all that. That's not too infantile.

686
00:47:59,800 --> 00:48:05,800
So I say, am I living that? What is happening?

687
00:48:05,800 --> 00:48:09,800
And it gives me energy to live that way,

688
00:48:09,800 --> 00:48:12,800
because I have no burden of the others.

689
00:48:12,800 --> 00:48:15,800
I don't know.

690
00:48:16,800 --> 00:48:17,800
Right?

691
00:48:17,800 --> 00:48:18,800
A. This is very, very remarkable.

692
00:48:18,800 --> 00:48:26,800
It reminds me of a story that is told about a swordsman

693
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:30,800
and his three sons.

694
00:48:30,800 --> 00:48:36,800
And it was an old, old swordsman in old Japan,

695
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:43,800
and he wanted to pass on the responsibility for his art to his sons.

696
00:48:43,800 --> 00:48:49,800
And he asked the sons, each, to come into his room,

697
00:48:49,800 --> 00:48:53,800
and he would speak to them, and he would decide.

698
00:48:53,800 --> 00:48:54,800
K. Good, good.

699
00:48:54,800 --> 00:48:58,800
A. He was a man of knowledge in terms of the sword,

700
00:48:58,800 --> 00:49:02,800
but he also was a man of understanding.

701
00:49:02,800 --> 00:49:10,800
And unbeknownst to them, he put a ball on the top of the lintel,

702
00:49:10,800 --> 00:49:14,800
and as they passed in, they, of course, were quite unaware of that.

703
00:49:14,800 --> 00:49:20,800
The youngest was called in first, and when the youngest walked in,

704
00:49:20,800 --> 00:49:23,800
his father had arranged for this ball to drop, you see,

705
00:49:23,800 --> 00:49:27,800
and the ball dropped, and the son, in a flash,

706
00:49:27,800 --> 00:49:31,800
cut it in two with his sword, and it fell down.

707
00:49:31,800 --> 00:49:35,800
And his father said, Please wait in the other room.

708
00:49:35,800 --> 00:49:37,800
The second son came in.

709
00:49:37,800 --> 00:49:41,800
The ball fell on his head, but precisely as it touched his head,

710
00:49:41,800 --> 00:49:43,800
he reached up and he took it in his hands,

711
00:49:43,800 --> 00:49:46,800
and father said, Please wait in the other room.

712
00:49:46,800 --> 00:49:50,800
The eldest son came in, he opened the door,

713
00:49:50,800 --> 00:49:55,800
and as he opened the door, he reached up and he took the ball.

714
00:49:55,800 --> 00:50:01,800
And the father called him in, and he read out the youngest son,

715
00:50:01,800 --> 00:50:04,800
and he said, Very brilliant.

716
00:50:04,800 --> 00:50:06,800
You've mastered the technique.

717
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:09,800
Don't understand anything.

718
00:50:09,800 --> 00:50:14,800
Said to the second one, Well, you're almost there.

719
00:50:14,800 --> 00:50:19,800
Just keep on, keep on.

720
00:50:19,800 --> 00:50:25,800
And he said to the eldest son, Well, now you can begin.

721
00:50:25,800 --> 00:50:31,800
And it seemed to me, that's just exactly imagined.

722
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:33,800
It's like the word prajna,

723
00:50:33,800 --> 00:50:41,800
which means, pra, ahead, jna, to know, to know beforehand,

724
00:50:41,800 --> 00:50:47,800
in the sense, not of some work of prediction that we do

725
00:50:47,800 --> 00:50:51,800
based on the study of rats in the lab or something.

726
00:50:51,800 --> 00:50:56,800
Yes, understanding is ahead and behind

727
00:50:56,800 --> 00:50:59,800
in the total movement of that one act.

728
00:50:59,800 --> 00:51:02,800
Oh yes, of course.

729
00:51:02,800 --> 00:51:05,800
So, I see this,

730
00:51:05,800 --> 00:51:11,800
because I do not separate meditation from daily living,

731
00:51:11,800 --> 00:51:13,800
otherwise it's no meaning.

732
00:51:13,800 --> 00:51:21,800
So I see the importance of order during the waking hours,

733
00:51:21,800 --> 00:51:30,800
and therefore freeing the mind from the brain from conflict,

734
00:51:30,800 --> 00:51:33,800
all that, during sleep.

735
00:51:33,800 --> 00:51:40,800
So there is total rest to the brain.

736
00:51:40,800 --> 00:51:42,800
That's one thing.

737
00:51:42,800 --> 00:51:49,800
Then, what is control?

738
00:51:49,800 --> 00:51:52,800
Why should I control?

739
00:51:52,800 --> 00:51:56,800
They have all said control.

740
00:51:56,800 --> 00:51:59,800
All religions have said control.

741
00:51:59,800 --> 00:52:02,800
Control, be without desire,

742
00:52:02,800 --> 00:52:06,800
don't think about yourself, you follow? All that.

743
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:11,800
I say to myself, this is what they say.

744
00:52:11,800 --> 00:52:16,800
Can I live without control?

745
00:52:16,800 --> 00:52:17,800
You follow, sir?

746
00:52:17,800 --> 00:52:18,800
A. Oh yes, yes.

747
00:52:18,800 --> 00:52:21,800
One has to start that question too, at the very beginning.

748
00:52:21,800 --> 00:52:23,800
K. I am doing it, that's what we are doing.

749
00:52:23,800 --> 00:52:26,800
A. Yes, my statement is a reflection, just a mirror to that.

750
00:52:26,800 --> 00:52:27,800
K. Yes.

751
00:52:27,800 --> 00:52:29,800
Am I...

752
00:52:29,800 --> 00:52:34,800
Is it possible to live without control?

753
00:52:34,800 --> 00:52:40,800
Because what is control? And who is the controller?

754
00:52:40,800 --> 00:52:45,800
The controller is the controlled.

755
00:52:45,800 --> 00:52:49,800
When I say, I must control my thought,

756
00:52:49,800 --> 00:52:55,800
the controller is the creation of thought.

757
00:52:55,800 --> 00:52:59,800
And thought controls thought, it has no meaning.

758
00:52:59,800 --> 00:53:03,800
One fragment controls another fragment,

759
00:53:03,800 --> 00:53:09,800
and yet, therefore, remain fragments.

760
00:53:09,800 --> 00:53:16,800
So I say, is there a way of living without control?

761
00:53:17,800 --> 00:53:23,800
Therefore no conflict, therefore no opposites,

762
00:53:23,800 --> 00:53:26,800
not one desire against another desire,

763
00:53:26,800 --> 00:53:30,800
one thought opposed to another thought,

764
00:53:30,800 --> 00:53:38,800
one achievement opposed to another achievement.

765
00:53:38,800 --> 00:53:43,800
So no control. Is that possible?

766
00:53:43,800 --> 00:53:45,800
Because I must find out.

767
00:53:45,800 --> 00:53:50,800
It's not just asking a question, just leaving it alone.

768
00:53:50,800 --> 00:53:53,800
I've got energy now,

769
00:53:53,800 --> 00:53:57,800
because I am not carrying their burden any more,

770
00:53:57,800 --> 00:54:00,800
nor am I carrying my own burden,

771
00:54:00,800 --> 00:54:03,800
because their burden is my burden.

772
00:54:03,800 --> 00:54:07,800
When I discard that, I discard this.

773
00:54:07,800 --> 00:54:09,800
So I've got energy.

774
00:54:09,800 --> 00:54:14,800
And I say, is it possible to live without control?

775
00:54:14,800 --> 00:54:18,800
And so there is a tremendous thing.

776
00:54:18,800 --> 00:54:20,800
I must find out,

777
00:54:20,800 --> 00:54:22,800
because the people who have control,

778
00:54:22,800 --> 00:54:24,800
they have said, through control,

779
00:54:24,800 --> 00:54:29,800
you arrive at nirvana, heaven,

780
00:54:29,800 --> 00:54:34,800
to me that's wrong, totally absurd.

781
00:54:34,800 --> 00:54:39,800
So I say, can I live a life of meditation

782
00:54:39,800 --> 00:54:43,800
in which there is no control?

783
00:54:46,800 --> 00:54:49,800
A. When intelligence breaks out,

784
00:54:49,800 --> 00:54:54,800
as we looked at before,

785
00:54:54,800 --> 00:54:59,800
then with it comes order.

786
00:54:59,800 --> 00:55:01,800
And that order... K. Intelligence is order.

787
00:55:01,800 --> 00:55:03,800
A. And intelligence is that order.

788
00:55:03,800 --> 00:55:05,800
The seeing is the doing.

789
00:55:05,800 --> 00:55:09,800
Therefore there is no conflict at all.

790
00:55:09,800 --> 00:55:11,800
K. Therefore do I live a life,

791
00:55:11,800 --> 00:55:16,800
not only is it possible, do I live it?

792
00:55:16,800 --> 00:55:19,800
I've got desires.

793
00:55:19,800 --> 00:55:25,800
I see a car, a woman, a house, a lovely garden,

794
00:55:25,800 --> 00:55:32,800
a beautiful clothes, or whatever it is.

795
00:55:33,800 --> 00:55:39,800
And instantly all the desires arise.

796
00:55:39,800 --> 00:55:46,800
And not to have a conflict, and yet not yield.

797
00:55:47,800 --> 00:55:51,800
If I have the money, I go and buy it,

798
00:55:51,800 --> 00:55:55,800
which is obvious, because that's no answer.

799
00:55:55,800 --> 00:55:58,800
If I have no money, I say, well, I'm so sorry, I have no money,

800
00:55:58,800 --> 00:56:00,800
and I will get some time, some day,

801
00:56:00,800 --> 00:56:03,800
I'll then come back and buy it.

802
00:56:03,800 --> 00:56:04,800
It's the same problem.

803
00:56:04,800 --> 00:56:07,800
But the desire is aroused,

804
00:56:07,800 --> 00:56:12,800
the seeing, contact, sensation, and desire.

805
00:56:12,800 --> 00:56:18,800
Now, that desire is there.

806
00:56:19,800 --> 00:56:25,800
And to cut it off is to suppress it.

807
00:56:26,800 --> 00:56:31,800
To control it is to suppress it.

808
00:56:31,800 --> 00:56:35,800
To yield to it is another form

809
00:56:35,800 --> 00:56:43,800
of fragmenting life into getting and losing.

810
00:56:43,800 --> 00:56:44,800
I don't know if I...

811
00:56:44,800 --> 00:56:46,800
A. Yes, yes, yes.

812
00:56:46,800 --> 00:56:59,800
K. So, to allow for the flowering of desire without control.

813
00:57:00,800 --> 00:57:02,800
You understand, sir? A. Yes, I do.

814
00:57:02,800 --> 00:57:07,800
K. So, the very flowering is the ending of that desire.

815
00:57:07,800 --> 00:57:13,800
But if you chop it off, it will come back again.

816
00:57:13,800 --> 00:57:14,800
Right, sir?

817
00:57:14,800 --> 00:57:18,800
A. Yes, it's the difference between a terminus and a consummation.

818
00:57:18,800 --> 00:57:24,800
K. So, I let the desire come, flower and watch it.

819
00:57:24,800 --> 00:57:28,800
Watch it, not yield or resist.

820
00:57:28,800 --> 00:57:33,800
Just let it flower

821
00:57:33,800 --> 00:57:40,800
and be fully aware of what is happening.

822
00:57:40,800 --> 00:57:44,800
Then there is no control.

823
00:57:44,800 --> 00:57:45,800
A. And no disorder.

824
00:57:45,800 --> 00:57:46,800
K. No, of course.

825
00:57:46,800 --> 00:57:50,800
The moment you control, there is a disorder.

826
00:57:50,800 --> 00:57:53,800
Because you are suppressing, or all the rest of it.

827
00:57:53,800 --> 00:57:54,800
So, that is disorder.

828
00:57:54,800 --> 00:58:00,800
But when you allow the thing to flower and watch it,

829
00:58:00,800 --> 00:58:06,800
watch it in the sense, be totally aware of it,

830
00:58:07,800 --> 00:58:12,800
the petals, the subtle forms of desire,

831
00:58:12,800 --> 00:58:14,800
to possess, not to possess,

832
00:58:14,800 --> 00:58:16,800
to possess is a pleasure, not to possess is a pleasure.

833
00:58:16,800 --> 00:58:17,800
You follow?

834
00:58:17,800 --> 00:58:20,800
The whole of that movement of desire.

835
00:58:20,800 --> 00:58:21,800
A. Exactly.

836
00:58:21,800 --> 00:58:26,800
K. And that you have to have a very sensitive watchfulness,

837
00:58:26,800 --> 00:58:31,800
very sensitive, choiceless watching.

838
00:58:31,800 --> 00:58:35,800
A. This image that you have referred to metaphorically

839
00:58:35,800 --> 00:58:37,800
with the plant itself.

840
00:58:37,800 --> 00:58:41,800
Could we pursue that in our next conversation

841
00:58:41,800 --> 00:58:44,800
through a continuation of concern

842
00:58:44,800 --> 00:58:46,800
to look further into meditation?

843
00:58:46,800 --> 00:58:47,800
K. Yes, we haven't finished meditation yet.

844
00:58:47,800 --> 00:58:49,800
There is lots more involved.

845
00:58:49,800 --> 00:58:51,800
A. Good.
